fread:
```c
size_t fread(void *ptr, size_t size, size_t nmemb, FILE *f) {
    if (!f) return 0;
    size_t want = size * nmemb;
    if (f->fd == -1 || want == 0) return 0;
    long n = my_syscall(0, f->fd, (unsigned int)ptr, (unsigned int)want);
    if (n <= 0) { f->eof = 1; if (n < 0) { f->err = 1; errno = EIO; } return 0; }
    f->pos += n;
    if (n < (long)want) f->eof = 1;
    return n / size;
}
```
Note: the VM's read returns -1 if fd is not in the cache (e.g., a closed fd) — handled.

Hmm — one important detail: in the VM, `this.fileDescriptors[this.registers[4]]` — register 4 = fd (a VM-internal fd index 0..N, not the host fd!). My C code uses fd values returned by the open syscall (VM's fdCounter). Consistent — I use the returned number as the fd. Good.

fwrite:
```c
size_t fwrite(const void *ptr, size_t size, size_t nmemb, FILE *f) {
    if (!f) return 0;
    size_t want = size * nmemb;
    long n = my_syscall(1, f->fd, (unsigned int)ptr, (unsigned int)want);
    if (n < 0) { f->err = 1; errno = EIO; return 0; }
    f->pos += n;
    return n / size;
}
```
