Hmm — for SEEK_END I need the file size: lseek(fd, 0, SEEK_END) returns the size (in the VM's cached case: fileSize + offset... wait, the VM: case 2 (SEEK_END): newPosition = fileSize + offset). So:
```c
int fseek(FILE *f, long offset, int origin) {
    long r;
    if (origin == SEEK_SET) r = my_syscall(8, f->fd, offset, 0);
    else if (origin == SEEK_END) r = my_syscall(8, f->fd, offset, 2);
    else r = my_syscall(8, f->fd, offset, 1);
    if (r < 0) return -1;
    f->pos = r; f->eof = 0;
    return 0;
}
```
Note: the VM's lseek SEEK_CUR: `fileInfo.position + offset` — it uses the VM's own position tracking (which is updated on read/write), not my f->pos. These stay in sync, since I update f->pos on every read/write and the VM does the same. For O_APPEND writes, the VM sets position = data.length on every write — my f->pos += n also tracks it. OK, consistent enough.

